# Binaries
testreg
/testreg
# Only the top-level `grunnr` binary (`go build .`) — anchored so it does
# NOT match the `cmd/grunnr/` package directory.
#
# `/atlas` is kept beside it: a working tree that predates the rename still
# has the old binary sitting at the root, and un-ignoring it the day the
# constant changed is how a 50 MB executable gets committed by `git add -A`.
/grunnr
/atlas
*.exe
*.exe~
*.dll
*.so
*.dylib

# Test binary, built with `go test -c`
*.test

# Output of the go coverage tool
*.out
coverage.html
# ...except checked-in coverage fixtures, which are test data, not build
# output. A coverprofile committed under a testdata/ directory is an input a
# test asserts against, and `*.out` swallowing one is a failure that only shows
# up in CI: the file is present on the machine that generated it, so the local
# suite passes and the pushed branch does not. It has cost this repo two
# debugging sessions (the attribution fixture, then the control-flow one).
#
# Anything under a testdata/ directory is therefore un-ignored, whatever its
# extension. New fixtures should also prefer a .coverprofile suffix, which no
# build-output rule claims in the first place.
!**/testdata/**

# Go workspace file
go.work
go.work.sum

# IDE
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
*.swo
*~

# OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Temporary files
*.tmp
*.bak

# Build output
/dist/
/bin/
.testreg-cache/
node_modules/

# Design canvases: the .dc.html artboards and canvas.json are source and are
# tracked; the seeded single-file canvas is a 3 MB build artifact.
#
# Both spellings: canvases seeded before the rename are named atlas-*, ones
# seeded after are grunnr-*. Dropping the old pattern would un-ignore a 2.7 MB
# artifact that is already on disk in every existing checkout.
.design/**/grunnr-*.html
.design/**/atlas-*.html
.design/**/docs-that-fail-ci.html

# `grunnr onboard` writes its provisional capability map here on every run,
# including the runs this repo's own docs are recorded from. It is a derived
# proposal set, regenerated from scratch each time, so it is not committed
# here — a project that wants its proposals in review can un-ignore it.
.grunnr/provisional/

# Agent worktrees live inside the repo and would otherwise be committed as
# embedded repositories — and would be matched by ./... in go test and lint.
.claude/worktrees/
